  "reading": "できし",
  "romaji": "dekishi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "death by drowning; drowning",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "death by drowning; drowning",
      "explanation": "Death caused by submersion in water or other liquid, resulting in the inability to breathe."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25916_dekishi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{溺死|できし}{事故|じこ}が{報告|ほうこく}された。",
      "english": "A drowning accident was reported.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25916_dekishi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{被害者|ひがいしゃ}の{死因|しいん}は{溺死|できし}と{判定|はんてい}された。",
      "english": "The victim's cause of death was determined to be drowning.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25916_dekishi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}の{溺死|できし}を{防|ふせ}ぐために、プールでは{必|かなら}ず{監視員|かんしいん}が{配置|はいち}されている。",
      "english": "To prevent children from drowning, lifeguards are always stationed at the pool.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {溺|でき} (drowning) + {死|し} (death). A formal, clinical term used in news reports, medical contexts, and legal proceedings. The everyday way to express the concept is {溺|おぼ}れて{死|し}ぬ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {溺死|できし}{事故|じこ}: drowning accident\n- {溺死|できし}{体|たい}: drowned body\n- {溺死|できし}する: to drown (to death)\n- {溺死|できし}を{防|ふせ}ぐ: to prevent drowning\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {溺|おぼ}れる: to drown; to nearly drown — the general verb, doesn't necessarily imply death\n- {水死|すいし}: death by drowning — a synonym; slightly less formal\n- {入水|じゅすい}: drowning oneself — specifically suicide by entering water",
